# Tutorial 09 — sun, saved cameras, render presets and a final image.
title: Rendering
summary: Sun position, render presets, saved cameras and a final render to an image
---
open sample "Cedar House"
caption "Saved cameras" "CAMERA restores the views saved with the project"
click mode 3D
camera Front
wait 2
camera Aerial
wait 2
camera Corner
wait 2
caption "The sun" "SUNSTUDY: date and time sliders; the shadows follow the solar position"
type SUNSTUDY
wait 4
type SUNSTUDY
caption "Your own camera" "Orbit to a view you like and SAVECAMERA it"
orbit 25 3
type SAVECAMERA "Garden view"
wait 1
caption "Render settings" "RENDER opens the render window: presets from Draft to Print 4K"
type RENDER
wait 4
caption "Render" "Sky, sun, exposure, ambient occlusion and soft shadows"
click button "Render" in "Render"
wait 8
close "Render"
caption "Render to a file" "RENDERTOFILE: size, pass, style and the image path"
camera Front
type RENDERTOFILE 1920x1080 Beauty Photographic ; $TMP/cedar-front.png
wait 2
note "Saved as a 1920 × 1080 PNG" top for 3
wait 3
caption "Next: sheets and PDF" "Tutorial 10 lays out drawings on paper"
wait 3
